# Verified scope

Added runtime_compaction_control.py and queue-preserving guards at terminal/socket,
router body append, app-server steer/start, terminal polling, and direct socket
handoff. Native compact and direct user recovery requests remain usable. External
pending backlog is not cleared, marked failed/delivered, or cursor-committed while
pressure is paused. Existing submitted wake confirmation timers exclude the pause.

Automatic compact reserves only an empty single-slot command repository; manual
new_session/goal_clear is never overwritten. Commands are deduplicated by session
and launch epoch. Submitted/RPC accepted is not completed. Admission requires a
new persisted native checkpoint AND a smaller below-budget next raw request.
Uncertain submission stays blocked; definite pre-submit failure has bounded retry
and cooldown. Checkpoint parser uses observed Claude 2.1.303 compact_boundary and
Codex 0.158 compacted replacement_history shapes from native-e2e/baseline-01.
The parser is bounded to 512 KiB tail bytes and never scans giant JSONL lines.

# Verification evidence

[Focused test output](evidence/controller/focused-tests.txt) records the isolated
focused selection. Inherited runtime/provider/client environment variables were
removed before imports, scripts.run_test_group.isolate_runtime_state was called,
and no external provider or live router endpoints were used. Includes actual
private durable state and JSONL checkpoint handoff, same pending backlog held
until proof then delivered once, wrong-session/old/quoted checkpoint rejection,
manual priority, uncertainty timeout, epoch scope, busy socket gate and direct
fallback preservation. Scoped ruff and compile checks also passed.

# Explicit integration boundary

Support implementation is not a complete live product recovery. Parent must
compose one shared private state path with build_runtime_compaction_control,
provide exact active session id plus common launch epoch across router/consumer,
call observe_request before guard/channel append, and pass compaction into
ChannelPendingIoPorts, ChannelTerminalPolicyPorts, CodexDesktopChannelPorts.
The factory accepts transcript_path callback; use the exact bound session file,
not an unrelated latest transcript. Raw count must be the same unmodified-stage
count across observations, never a post-guard count. Proven overflow can call
observe_request(..., recovery_required=True). Native compact detection must reuse
compact_request_kind from context_summary_policy; no new heuristic is introduced.

No live session, SSE receiver, backlog cursor, install, restart or commit was
performed by this task. Native CLI E2E and screenshots belong to the parent native
verification task and are not claimed by this journal.
